  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Find the value of $\\sqrt{12}\\cdot \\sqrt{12}.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we re-write the expression as a square:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{12}\\cdot \\sqrt{12}={(\\sqrt{12})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, recall that the square and the square root cancel each other out. So, we have\n\n$$\n{(\\sqrt{12})}^{2}=12.\n$$",
